import GroupLean.Coord

/-!
# Theorem E: functional relations over three letters

For each of the `3^9 = 19683` maps `g : Fin 3 → Fin 3 → Fin 3`, the relation
`P_g a b c :↔ g a b = c` is representable over `ℤ^k`, `(ZMod 2)^k` or `(ZMod 3)^k` (explicit
equation system), or has a one-coordinate OV gadget; never both.

The maps are the words `w ∈ words 3 9` (`g a b = w[3a+b]`). The table `fun3Table` (16-bit
entries, one per word) and `fun3Reps` (297 equation systems) were generated by a script that is
not part of this repository (the kernel checks them, so it need not be trusted); `fun3Chunk_0` … `fun3Chunk_19` check all 19683 certificates (in chunks of 1000) by
kernel reduction (`decide +kernel`, no extra axioms).
-/

namespace GroupLean

/-- The functional relation of a word of 9 letters: `(a,b,c) ∈ P ↔ w[3a+b] = c`. -/
def relF (w : List ℕ) (a b c : ℕ) : Bool := w.getD (3 * a + b) 0 == c

